    <tags>serv service supervisor nssm windows systemd launchd process-manager yaml cli</tags>
    <summary>Install and supervise long-running executables as native OS services (Windows SCM / systemd / launchd).</summary>
    <description>serv installs and supervises a long-running executable as a native Windows service (via the Service Control Manager), or a systemd/launchd unit on Linux/macOS. It is a cross-platform, modern alternative to tools like NSSM, adding process lifecycle management, graceful shutdown, automatic restart with backoff, stdout/stderr capture with rotation, and lifecycle hooks - all driven by one YAML config that works the same way on every platform.

This package downloads the official serv.exe binary for your architecture from the TillmanBuildsTech/serv GitHub release and verifies its SHA256 checksum before installing. It is a portable install: serv.exe is placed on your PATH (via a Chocolatey shim) and does not require Administrator privileges to run.</description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/TillmanBuildsTech/serv/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</releaseNotes>
    <copyright>Copyright (c) Tillman Builds Tech</copyright>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
